{
  "_comment": "Peak keywords found in YAMAP / Yamareco / Strava titles, resolved to the English name the site prints. The build script scans each title for these keywords and names the outing after the highest one it finds; a title with no keyword falls back to `unnamed` and is listed by the script so an entry can be added here. `m` is the usual published summit height. `hyaku` ties the keyword to _data/hikes/hyakumeizan.json. `not` lists words that cancel the keyword for that title, because Japanese peak names nest (経ヶ岳 inside 八経ヶ岳, 剣山 inside 八剣山, 男体山 inside 筑波山(男体山)) and the inner name wins whenever it is the taller mountain.",
