      "_why": "経ヶ岳 is one of Fuji's 八神峰, and YAMAP puts it in the title of a Yoshida-route day. Both 経ヶ岳 outings here start at the Subaru Line fifth station (2305 m) and top out on the crater rim, so the keyword means Fuji on this site. Nagano's own 経ヶ岳 (2296 m) has not been walked; give it its own keyword — 大泉所岳 or the like — if it ever is, because a bare 経ヶ岳 cannot tell the two apart."
